  "conclusions": [
    {
      "owner": "LegacyPlayerProgression",
      "finding": "Current source matches corrected contract. Distinct server players plus same UUID gated before writes; both death and End-return Clone admitted. Independent static literal/finite-loop enumeration found107 keys matching contract, no missing/extra/type mismatch. Native contains(key,non99) exact types and UUID length4 checked.",
      "alias": "Typed root copy precedes ten-key typed true OR from OLD root/nested to NEW ROOT only. No nested write or reward dispatch. Existing whole-container copiers cannot overwrite repaired root; former CLONE-ALIAS-ORDER P1 resolved.",
      "economic": "Exact valid Long/Int pair copied raw without rebase. Malformed/partial diagnostic skip is explicitly outside anti-reset guarantee. Former CLONE-CAP-PARTIAL overclaim resolved by stated limit; malformed budget behavior itself is NOT fixed or certified safe.",
      "ownership": "No whole root copy, other-owner keys untouched, School/Army/Secret/Slot handlers and guide/warm resets not duplicated. tag.copy used; primitive immutable sharing is legal."
    },
    {
      "owner": "LegacyItemMappings",
      "finding": "Forge bus, item registry, dynasty namespace and two explicit old IDs only. Canonical target must be registered, nonAIR and exact key. Unknown mappings untouched.",
      "targets": "quest_ledger prefers registered ftbquests:book; actual cached1.20.1 FTB registers BOOK and use opens GUI client side without awards. Missing FTB target falls back registered dynasty_guide with warning. healing_talisman maps registered vajra_talisman matching current historical replacement comment; no healing behavior recreated.",
      "native": "MissingMappingsEvent validates target registered in ACTIVE pool; GameData posts Forge bus and processes STAGING then validates/copies ACTIVE. ForgeRegistry REMAP removes missing, attempts old numeric ID and installs oldname->canonical alias. Alias getValue/getRaw and defaulted-wrapper ItemStack lookup are bound.",
      "limits": "Exact old numeric ID NOT guaranteed: native add can return existing target ID and warn. Handler grants no new stack. Native ItemStack loads Count/tag/ForgeCaps through standard verifyTagAfterLoad/forgeInit hooks, which may normalize; exact legacy custom data durability requires real isolated-world load/save/reopen. Unresolved DEFAULT is not accepted compatibility."
    }
  ],
